//! The marks SMOOTH draws, as Phosphor outlines.
//!
//! Phosphor Icons (https://phosphoricons.com), MIT licensed. The path data is
//! embedded rather than shipped as a font, so a glyph is a shape the compiler
//! checks: it scales to any box, tints with any ink, and needs no codepoint.
//!
//! The editor's marks are solid -- headphones, the gear, the padlock -- so most
//! of these are the fill weight. The arrows and the globe are the bold weight:
//! at the size the toolbar draws them, the regular weight's stroke all but
//! disappears.

